<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yasinia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kőrösmező</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yasinia is a mountain settlement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-ruthenia">Zakarpattia</a> oblast, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, near the source of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a>. Formerly part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, it was the centre of the short-lived Hutsul Republic of 1918-1919, until Romanian troops occupied it in June 1919. It is now a centre for tourism and skiing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yasinia.jpg" alt="Yasinia" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Varga Attila · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yasinia_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
